=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_4c7d — Standard split, dinner at 20 (fork of p_a1b2)

Forked from p_a1b2 to correct the dinner window. The 18:00 pass shows plate_elena in the cupboard and glass_priya in the sink; the 20:00 pass shows plate_elena at the dining table (3 sightings) and glass_priya at the dining table (2 sightings). Dinner is 19:30–21:00, not 18:30–20:00. The lunch window (12:00–13:30) is unchanged. All other blocks and the commute picture are identical to the parent.

Elena leaves for her office around 8:00 on weekdays and returns at 17:30. Her laptop, backpack, wallet, hat, helmet, bike lock, and umbrella all go out with her. Priya is home most of the day, takes a morning walk 7:00–8:00, and runs afternoon errands 14:00–16:00. The dog is fed by Priya at 7:30 (bowl at the kitchen floor) and walked by Elena in the evening 18:00–19:00. Meals are at the dining table: lunch 12:00–13:30, dinner 19:30–21:00. Evening TV runs 20:00–22:30 with the remote, blanket, and fruit bowl on the coffee table. Priya plays guitar in the bedroom 21:00–22:00. Elena bakes on Saturday mornings 9:00–12:00. Priya showers 6:30–7:30; Elena showers 21:30–22:30.

What sets this hypothesis apart from the parent: the dining table is bare of plates and glasses at 18:00 (they are still in the cupboard) and only set by 19:30. What would refute it: plates at the dining table at 18:00 or 18:30 on a weekday, or the laptop in the house between 9:00 and 17:00 on a weekday.

